<div class="sheet-header stonetop-sheet-header">
	{{!-- The slot is what the crop pip positions against; the portrait keeps its own sizing.

	      NO data-edit: it is how ActorSheet binds Foundry's file picker to an image, and that
	      binding is registered before ours and cannot be called off from a listener — so while it
	      was here, clicking the portrait in edit mode could only ever reach the raw file browser.
	      The People of Stonetop gallery carries "Browse files…" and "Use default" of its own, so
	      it is a superset of what the attribute bought. --}}
	<span class="stonetop-portrait-slot">
		{{#if stonetop.portraitFramed}}
		{{!-- A framed portrait needs a clipping box: the image is absolutely positioned at
		      several hundred percent, so with nothing to clip it, it paints across the sheet. The
		      box wears .stonetop-portrait — it is the portrait now, and that class carries the
		      size, the border and the click that opens the window. Only this branch is new; an
		      unframed portrait stays the bare <img> it has always been, which is what lets that
		      class's own top-anchored crop go on serving everyone nobody has framed. --}}
		<span class="stonetop-portrait stonetop-portrait-clip" title="{{actor.name}}">
			<img class="stonetop-portrait-img" src="{{stonetop.portraitImg}}" style="{{stonetop.portraitImgStyle}}" alt="{{actor.name}}">
		</span>
		{{else}}
		<img class="stonetop-portrait" src="{{actor.img}}" title="{{actor.name}}" alt="{{actor.name}}">
		{{/if}}
		{{> "stonetop.portrait-frame-pip" canFrame=stonetop.canFramePortrait canTokenize=stonetop.canTokenizePortrait}}
	</span>
	<div class="sheet-header__fields">
		{{#if (and isCharacter (not limited))}}
		<div class="stonetop-playbook-block">
			<div class="stonetop-playbook-row">
				{{!-- What this character IS, in one line. Normally that's the playbook and its
				      Instinct. Once they've died and come back wearing an insert, the insert IS
				      what they are — it replaces the playbook's name here and brings its own
				      Instinct, because "Ghost (Denial)" is the true answer and "The Heavy
				      (Loyal)" is who they used to be. The old pair stays, struck through and
				      small, beside it: nothing about them was deleted, and a Revenant is still a
				      Heavy underneath. --}}
				<span class="stonetop-playbook-drop-zone {{#unless stonetop.playbook.name}}empty{{/unless}}">
					{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert}}
					{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.name}}{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.badge}} <span class="stonetop-instinct-badge" data-tooltip="{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.badge.tooltip}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN">({{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.badge.word}})</span>{{/if}}
					{{else if stonetop.playbook.name}}
					{{stonetop.playbook.name}}{{#if stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge}} <span class="stonetop-instinct-badge" data-tooltip="{{stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge.tooltip}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN">({{stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge.word}})</span>{{/if}}
					{{else}}Drop a playbook here{{/if}}
				</span>
				{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert}}
				{{#if stonetop.playbook.name}}
				{{! The playbook goes grey the moment the insert lands — that identity IS replaced.
				    Its Instinct is a separate question and comes along only once the insert's own
				    Instinct has actually been chosen, which is the same gate the Details tab uses
				    for its "retired" note and its read-out. Between taking the insert and choosing
				    an Instinct (a state the walkthrough explicitly allows you to leave the window
				    in) the header used to strike out an Instinct the sheet was still using. }}
				<span class="stonetop-playbook-retired"
				      data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.retiredTooltip"}}" data-tooltip-direction="DOWN">
					<s>{{stonetop.playbook.name}}{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.selected}}{{#if stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge}} ({{stonetop.playbook.instinct.badge.word}}){{/if}}{{/if}}</s>
				</span>
				{{/if}}
				{{/if}}
			</div>
			{{#if stonetop.playbook.description}}
			<p class="stonetop-playbook-description">{{stonetop.playbook.description}}</p>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}
		<div class="stonetop-name-called-box">
			<div class="stonetop-name-called-inner">
				<span class="stonetop-name-called-label">I am called...</span>
				{{#if stonetop.editMode}}
				<input class="input--title stonetop-name-field" name="name" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" placeholder="Name"/>
				{{else}}
				<span class="input--title stonetop-header-locked stonetop-name-field">{{actor.name}}</span>
				{{/if}}
			</div>
		</div>
		{{#if stonetop.playbook.appearance.summary}}
		<p class="stonetop-appearance-summary">{{stonetop.playbook.appearance.summary}}</p>
		{{/if}}
	</div>
</div>
